---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { projects } from '../../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Projects">
  <div class="container page">
    <header class="page-header"><span class="eyebrow">Projects · {projects.length}</span><h1>Selected projects.</h1><p>Android applications, system tools, and experiments spanning application code, automation, and system integration.</p></header>
    <div class="grid project-list">
      {projects.map((project) => <a class="card project-card" href={project.href}>
        <div class="project-card-visual">
          {project.slug === 'killmyapps' && <img class="project-icon" src="/images/projects/KillMyAppsIcon.png" alt="KillMyApps icon" loading="lazy" />}
          {project.slug === 'dterminal' && <img class="project-icon" src="/images/projects/DTerminalIcon.png" alt="DTerminal icon" loading="lazy" />}
          {project.slug === 'evilfont' && <img class="project-icon" src="/images/projects/EvilFontIcon.png" alt="EvilFont icon" loading="lazy" />}
        </div>
        <div class="project-card-content">
          <div class="project-card-top"><span class="eyebrow">{project.category}</span><span class="status"><span class="status-dot"></span>{project.status}</span></div>
          <h2>{project.name}</h2><p>{project.description}</p>
          <div class="tags">{project.tags.map((tag) => <span class="tag">{tag}</span>)}</div>
          <div class="project-link">View details →</div>
        </div>
      </a>)}
    </div>
    <section class="section split-section">
      <div><span class="eyebrow">Engineering focus</span><h2>Closer to the platform.</h2></div>
      <div class="prose"><p>The projects cover different layers of Android, from Compose and application architecture to Root, Shizuku, native execution, automation, and performance.</p><p>The common thread is practical tooling: each project starts with a specific problem and keeps its implementation tied to that use case.</p></div>
    </section>
    <section class="section split-section">
      <div><span class="eyebrow">Across the stack</span><h2>Different tools for different layers.</h2></div>
      <div class="prose"><p>Depending on the problem, I use Kotlin and Compose, C/C++, Python, Bash, Android SDK/NDK APIs, or system-level interfaces. The choice follows the requirements of the project rather than a fixed stack.</p></div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
